       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1200 mg/day for OTC use.\n\nA dose this high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It would be unlikely to add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **800 mg PO three times daily** (2400 mg/day). This is a common regimen for inflammatory conditions or pain.\n2. **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n3. **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1600 mg/day). This is a typical dose for mild to moderate pain.\n4. **1600 mg/day total**, which may be what the \"1600\" meant, divided into doses such as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf the 1600 mg four times daily dose is deliberate, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
